<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ji'an, Jilin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ji'an is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jilin">Jilin province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Yalu river facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gungnae">Gungnae</a> it was the capital of Goguryeo for about four centuries, and its surroundings hold the stele of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwanggaeto-the-great">Gwanggaeto the Great</a> and thousands of Goguryeo tombs, including the stepped stone Tomb of the General. These remains were listed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> in 2004 together with sites at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huanren">Huanren</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ji-an-jilin.jpg" alt="Ji'an, Jilin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EditQ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ji%27an_Museum_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
